# react-query

- Centralize query keys in `src/api/queryKeys.ts` as factory objects:

```ts
export const queryKeys = {
  users: {
    all: ['users'] as const,
    list: (params: UserListParams) => [...queryKeys.users.all, 'list', params] as const,
    detail: (id: string) => [...queryKeys.users.all, 'detail', id] as const,
  },
};
```

- One hook per query/mutation in `api/` or feature `api/` folder (`useUsers`, `useCreateUser`)
- Set `staleTime` explicitly; use `enabled` guard when query depends on params
- Mutations: invalidate related keys in `onSuccess`; show errors via antd `message` or form feedback
- Never call `fetch` directly in components — always go through a hook
- Use `queryClient.setQueryData` for optimistic updates; roll back in `onError`
- Export hook return types when consumed by multiple components

For good/bad examples, read `examples/rules/react-query.md` when applying this rule.
